# Keep project docs updated

This repo uses living docs at the root:

- `Agents.md` — agent entrypoint
- `Memory.md` — handoff log (always touch on non-trivial work)
- `PRD.md`, `Architecture.md`, `Rules.md`, `Phases.md`, `Design.md`

## When you make changes

After implementing or fixing something non-trivial (features, architecture, APIs, UI system, phases, conventions):

1. Append a dated entry to `Memory.md` and refresh the “Current snapshot” / gaps if needed.
2. Patch any other living doc whose domain changed (don’t leave stale function names, secrets, or phase status).
3. Keep edits concise — correct the facts; don’t rewrite the whole file unless necessary.

## When you start a session

Prefer reading `Agents.md` + `Memory.md` before exploring the whole codebase.

## Do not

- Skip `Memory.md` after meaningful work
- Duplicate large README content into these docs
- Commit secrets into any doc
